I look at the menu on the counter.
There are many items there.
But I want a cutting chai.
And I also want a bun maska.
I speak to the uncle.
"Uncle, is a cutting chai available?" I ask.
"And a classic bun maska too?"
He looks at me and smiles.
He warmly nods his head.
"Yes Madam, it is definitely available," he says.
"Do you want anything else?"
"No, just this much for now," I reply.
I ask him about the money.
"Shall I give the money now?"
"No Madam," the uncle tells me.
"You go inside."
"Sit at an empty table."
"Your order will come right there."
I say thank you to him.
And I go towards the inside.
